LIKEOS-BOOTMENU.CONF(5)          File Formats          LIKEOS-BOOTMENU.CONF(5)

NAME
       likeos-bootmenu.conf - the boot menu of the LikeOS installation medium

SYNOPSIS
       \EFI\LIKEOS\bootmenu.conf on the EFI system partition

DESCRIPTION
       The  LikeOS boot loader (BOOTX64.EFI) shows a menu before it starts the
       kernel when the EFI system partition it was loaded from  has  the  file
       \EFI\LIKEOS\bootmenu.conf.   The  USB  medium  LikeOS is written to has
       one, with the entries Run LikeOS Live from USB and Install LikeOS  from
       USB; a LikeOS installed on a disk has none, and starts straight away.

       The  menu  is  drawn  on  the firmware's graphics screen (as text where
       there is none).  Up and Down choose an entry, Home and  End  the  first
       and  the  last,  a  digit the entry of that number (1 the first); Enter
       starts the chosen entry.  Until a key is pressed a countdown runs,  and
       when it ends the default entry starts.

       The  file  is  UTF-8 text, one setting per line.  Lines starting with #
       are comments; empty lines are ignored; blanks around  a  line  are  ig-
       nored.

       timeout=seconds
              How long the menu waits before it starts the default entry.

       default=index
              The  entry  chosen  when  the  menu appears and started when the
              countdown ends, counted from 0 in the order of the  entry  lines
              (default 0, the first).

       title=text
              The heading of the menu.

       entry=title|words
              One  menu  entry,  in  the order of the file: the title the menu
              shows, a vertical bar, and the words the entry adds to the  ker-
              nel command line (they may be empty).  The kernel and the system
              it starts see them in /proc/cmdline.

KERNEL COMMAND LINE WORDS
       likeos.mode=install
              init(8) starts LikeOS Setup, likeos-installer(1), on the console
              instead  of  the login prompt (it reads /etc/inittab.install in-
              stead of /etc/inittab).

       efi=noruntime
              The kernel does not call the  firmware's  runtime  services:  no
              UEFI  variables  in /sys/firmware/efi/efivars (for firmware that
              misbehaves; boot entries cannot be changed then).

EXAMPLE
       The file on the USB medium:

              # The boot menu of the LikeOS USB medium
              title=LikeOS
              timeout=10
              default=0
              entry=Run LikeOS Live from USB|
              entry=Install LikeOS from USB|likeos.mode=install

SEE ALSO
       likeos-installer(1), likeos-install(1), likeos-efiboot(1)

